            "record_type": "agtxiv.v3.source-span/0.0.0",
            "revision": 1
          }
        ],
        "text": "The authors claim that stabilizer work, defined by a base-2 logarithmic ratio of core stabilizer partition functions, is faithful, Clifford invariant, subadditive, nonincreasing under discarding a factor of a pure product state, and invariant under adding stabilizer ancillas. They further use it as a monotone under deterministic pure-state stabilizer protocols. This is an unverified author-claim candidate."
      }
    ],
